    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257-a1">

                <pb facs="0365" n="247" xml:id="pg247"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Annex]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Embassy to the
                            Department of State</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Declaration</hi></p>
                <p>In view of the apprehension that the phrase “in the names of their respective
                    peoples” in Article 1 of the Treaty for the Renunciation of War, signed at Paris
                    on August 27, 1928, may convey a suggestion of incompatibility with the
                    provisions of the Imperial Constitution, the Japanese Government declare that,
                    so far as Japan is concerned, the said phrase is understood as having no
                    application in any constitutional signification.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
